{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24024 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Callyspongenol B appears to interact with Neuropilin-2 through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the enzyme Carboxylesterase 2 or Raji and HepG2 cells. The shared pathway of (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, a compound that targets Neuropilin-2, indicates a possible role in the regulation of this receptor. The evidence suggests that Callyspongenol B may influence Neuropilin-2 through a downstream effect, possibly by modulating the activity of these intermediate targets. The consistent presence of the same compound in the target list for Neuropilin-2 across different cell lines supports a functional link, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Callyspongenol B to exert its effects through a complex network involving enzyme activity and receptor regulation.",
